]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "`blastn` is **not** currently whitelisted. I’ll add it for you now so you’ll be able to run the alignment later. I’ll assign it “requires_approval” so the administrator can review it once before you execute it."}, {"role": "tool_call", "content": "{'name': 'super-shell-add_to_whitelist', 'arguments': '{"command": "blastn", "securityLevel": "requires_approval", "description": "BLAST nucleotide sequence database query program"}'}"}, {"role": "tool_response", "content": "Command 'blastn' added to whitelist with security level 'requires_approval'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "That’s all set—`blastn` is now on the whitelist with *requires_approval*.  
When you’re ready to run your `blastn -query sample.fasta -db nt -out results.txt` command, type it normally; the system will flag it for approval first (per the *requires_approval* setting). Once an administrator approves it, your alignment will execute on the cluster."}]
